# Line endings, pinned so a checkout behaves the same on every platform.
#
# A shell script stored with CRLF endings will not run on macOS or Linux: the
# kernel reads the shebang as "#!/usr/bin/env sh\r" and fails to find it.
# Windows launchers are the mirror image - cmd.exe is happiest with CRLF.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Everything else is normalised to LF in the repository and left alone in the
# working tree, so a Windows checkout does not rewrite every file as a diff.
* text=auto
